course: dictionary
lesson: 9352
title: Splendidly: grand, and excellent
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Splendidly is an adverb, so it tells you how someone does something. It comes from splendid, which means grand, bright or excellent. Splendidly can mean very well, or it can mean in a grand, rich and beautiful way.
explain: «The White Rabbit returns "splendidly dressed", with white kid gloves and a large fan.» The clues are the gloves, the fan and the word dressed. He is dressed in a smart, grand way, so splendidly means grandly and beautifully here.
explain: Now look at «You did splendidly!» Nobody is saying you were dressed up. They mean you did an excellent job. Check by swapping in another word: «You did excellently!» still makes sense, so the meaning is very well.
fact: Splendidly means very well, or excellently.
fact: Splendidly can also mean in a grand, rich and beautiful way.
fact: «Splendid» means grand, magnificent or excellent.
fact: «Splendidly dressed» means dressed in fine, grand clothes.
fact: Splendid is a little old-fashioned, and British writers and teachers often use it.
exercise: «You did splendidly in the test!» What does splendidly mean here? | Very slowly | Very angrily | *Very well | Only just
exercise: «The White Rabbit returns "splendidly dressed", with white kid gloves and a large fan.» What does splendidly dressed suggest? | Dressed in nothing but a hat | Dressed in old, torn rags | Dressed for a muddy walk in the rain | *Dressed in a grand, smart and beautiful way
exercise: Splendidly comes from another word. Which word is it? | *splendid | spindle | splinter | spelled
test: «The orchestra played splendidly, and the audience cheered.» What does splendidly mean? | Late and rushed | Sadly and slowly | *Excellently | Badly and noisily
test: Which word means the same as splendidly in the grand sense? | Sleepily | Hungrily | Crossly | *Magnificently
exam: The author says the White Rabbit is «splendidly dressed». What is the best reason for this word? | It shows he is very small and quiet | It shows he is lost in the woods | It shows he has forgotten his gloves | *It shows he looks grand and smart, not scruffy
